        "shortHash": "1d40fe519",
        "hash": "1d40fe5194396f8d62b13809b438fdd2f378d300",
        "subject": "feat(boundary): HISO-005 BUILD0245 parse .tsx as TSX in the B6 kernel (JSX refused in the domain)",
        "body": "feat(boundary): HISO-005 BUILD0245 parse .tsx as TSX in the B6 kernel (JSX refused in the domain)\n\nSPEC0245 T1/T2 (docs/02_spec/0245_b6_tsx_parse.md, approved by the user for\na local BUILD), on top of the main with BUILD0244 (PR #9).\n\n- T1: the ScriptKind follows a closed table by extension: .tsx -> TSX,\n  .jsx -> JSX, .ts/.mts/.cts -> TS, everything else -> JS (the TypeScript\n  default for the runtime extensions). It applies to the normal pass and to\n  the refusal census, which share the acquisition.\n- T2 has no code: the three JSX forms (JsxElement, JsxSelfClosingElement,\n  JsxFragment) fall into the existing expression fallback as\n  UNKNOWN_UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX with the SyntaxKind; attributes and children are\n  never evaluated. .tsx keeps UNKNOWN_FORMAT and UNKNOWN_MODULE_FORMAT, and\n  the acquisition still visits the real JSX subtree.\n- Limits, profile, recipes and the global proof rule are unchanged. Kernel\n  version semantic-kernel-v6-tsx-parse.\n\nThe kernel version literal is migrated in five B6 tests, as registered in the\ncontract. New test tests/b6-0245-tsx-parse.test.js (18 cases). On the\nevaluated root 228e7918, reconstituted with its 1,410 inputs checked, the B6\nmeasurement goes from 12,283 to 11,723 diagnostics: 561 tuples from the\nrecovered AST of the .tsx files disappear and 1 JsxElement refusal appears,\nwith zero change outside the .tsx files, 0 proofs and 0 violations, normal\nequal to strict. B6 stays INCOMPLETE.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
